---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use — LaunchPad"
  description="The house rules for using LaunchPad: free to use, education only, be decent, and what you can reuse."
  path=""
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container column prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        These are the house rules. They are written to be read, not skimmed past. If you are under
        18, it is worth reading them with a parent or guardian.
      </p>
      <p class="updated">Last updated {site.legalUpdated}.</p>

      <h2>What LaunchPad is</h2>
      <p>
        A free education site about money and business, run by {site.owner} as a non-commercial
        project. Using it costs nothing, and nothing on it is for sale.
      </p>

      <h2>Education, not advice</h2>
      <p>
        Everything here is general education. It is not financial, investment, legal, tax or
        accounting advice, and it does not know your situation. Before you act on anything
        involving real money, debt or a binding agreement, check the official source for your
        country and talk to someone qualified or an adult you trust. The
        <a href={`${base}/disclaimer`}>Disclaimer</a> says more.
      </p>

      <h2>Using the site</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You can read, share links to, print and use the lessons and calculators for yourself, your club or your class.</li>
        <li>Do not use the site to send spam, break the law, or harm other people.</li>
        <li>Do not try to break the site, overload it, or get around any protections.</li>
        <li>Do not present LaunchPad content as coming from a financial adviser or as a recommendation to buy or sell anything.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Reusing our work</h2>
      <p>
        Unless a page says otherwise, the text and lessons are licensed under
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Creative Commons BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>:
        share and adapt them for non-commercial use, credit LaunchPad, and share adaptations under
        the same licence. The site's code is open source under the MIT licence in the
        <a href={site.repo} rel="noopener noreferrer">repository</a>. Third-party material
        (statistics, quotations, linked documents) belongs to its owners and is cited.
      </p>

      <h2>Accounts, when they exist</h2>
      <p>
        There are no accounts today. If sign-in launches, it will be optional and covered by the
        <a href={`${base}/privacy`}>Privacy</a> page. You would be responsible for keeping your
        sign-in codes and sync codes private, and we could close an account that breaks these
        rules. You could delete your account at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>No guarantees</h2>
      <p>
        We work hard to keep everything accurate and up to date, and we fix mistakes when they are
        reported, but the site is provided as it is, without warranties. To the extent the law
        allows, LaunchPad and its author are not liable for losses that come from relying on the
        site. Nothing here limits rights you have as a consumer under the law where you live.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes and law</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms; the date above changes when we do, and the history is public in
        the repository. The project is based in New York, United States, and these terms are
        governed by its laws unless the law where you live says otherwise for consumers.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
